{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02GH", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\nSee for example \\cite[Remark 18.30 (2).]{GWII}.\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-permanence-better}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:be75474e53481ec03e53e62fa2cbe44bb530abded5ef59370b51a6ccbb96c7a6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:db59ab8f300f69cd3d7e2301af682b9853813030e2827b1cfc40f2eae82d6aea", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes over <MATH_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0003> is <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> is unramified over <MATH_0006>, then\n<MATH_0007> is <ACCENT_0002>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6e4c002fd5f2c81ab684f537dbf8d9715ecae5bc52b271be34d2370c17c11774", "unit_id": "tag:0HB1:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02GH", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$X \\to X \\times_S Y \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{id}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$Y \\to Y \\times_S Y$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & X \\times_S Y \\ar[d] \\\\\nY \\ar[r] & Y \\times_S Y\n}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$Y \\to Y \\times_S Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-composition-etale}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-etale}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-diagonal-unramified-morphism}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-base-change-immersion}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-open-immersion-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d01b0175be29ef6ed63b7b5c63bb66800e30e3f7de991258b7eeed96edb9d606", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:58253801acd76960f430a7b578453ee68ed93821156c43333d64e97290b59d24", "source_text": "Consider the factorization <MATH_0001>, where the first arrow\nis given by <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> and the second arrow is the projection.\nWe claim both arrows are <ACCENT_0001>tale and hence <MATH_0004> is <ACCENT_0002>tale by\nLemma <REF_0001>. Namely, the projection is <ACCENT_0003>tale\nas it is the base change of <MATH_0005>, see Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThe first arrow is the base change of the diagonal morphism\n<MATH_0006> because the square\n<MATH_0007>\nis cartesian. The diagonal <MATH_0008> is an open immersion by\nLemma <REF_0003>. The base change\nof an open immersion is an open immersion\n(Schemes, Lemma <REF_0004>)\nand an open immersion is <ACCENT_0004>tale\n(Lemma <REF_0005>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2e161c9ea1ffd6a87664c80ddd3239920e10839a97722baa75dfee6f97b71500", "unit_id": "tag:0HB1:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02GH", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nCancellation law for \\'etale morphisms\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2a6a64d5192260043e46e34429d0cfa1deaa99aad484061c909a10de83b02cbe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a5c670fa7de2f8391c0aaa2053e2fb6fb6a3d66259093e60b25c97f004865371", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes over <MATH_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0005>, then\n<MATH_0006> is <ACCENT_0002>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:022bb48c2e6ddc81d96d12cac1ed3d94b9cc54d37b792328da10553e0a30d36c", "unit_id": "tag:02GW:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02GH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Y \\to S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-etale-smooth-unramified}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-etale-permanence-better}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-map-between-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c2c4e49ec4a001ebaa1e48079cd3051653fe97888c545ffad034f9a4a0e5f8d3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c75e1cfa60728faa10445d604ee6e7fc1c231c0044aa978276037d4917bb3c38", "source_text": "Since <MATH_0001> is unramified by Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe may apply Lemma <REF_0002>. See also\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:93cdf2c97b3076d5920170baeb2d4aef669c027c2d8dd87c744c553f213eec05", "unit_id": "tag:02GW:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02GH", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[rr]_f \\ar[rd]_p & &\nY \\ar[dl]^q \\\\\n& S\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$p$", "MATH_0004": "$q$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$q$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{descent-lemma-flat-finitely-presented-permanence}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{descent-lemma-smooth-permanence}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-permanence-two}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:70f89f9a62a288c28e52269f35d6fbbaaab1c1526e6403fe61dfd193459f0145", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:98a5dbed213cb6951f58659c72f11d8d28f54046b0a6fd9abd74b69980a5c479", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes. Assume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is surjective, and <ACCENT_0001>tale,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is <ACCENT_0002>tale, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0004> is locally of finite presentation<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>In fact this\nis implied by (1) and (2), see\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nMoreover, it suffices to assume that <MATH_0005> is surjective, flat and\nlocally of finite presentation, see\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0002>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThen <MATH_0006> is <ACCENT_0003>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:71a55aed750e56ae938517303ac31086ddad1e25ae0dd20035b8e8cc4792294f", "unit_id": "tag:02K6:statement"}
